  "worked_solution": "The second-order Cauchy\u2013Euler equation has the form\n\n$$\na{t}^{2}y\u2032\u2032+bty\u2032+cy=f(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b,$ and $c$ are constants.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that has the above form is\n\n$$\n4{t}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}+3t{y}^{\u2032}-2y=t+1.\n$$",
